# Shared `bin/apq.js`. All flags live in bin/apq-js-common.hxml — the
# include path is resolved against the CWD, so build from the repo root.
bin/apq-js-common.hxml
-js bin/apq.js
# Then the code-cache launcher beside it (bin/apq-launch-common.hxml) and its
# cache, warmed through the shim so the warm run has the node flags a call
# has. A `--cmd`, never a `--next` block: a typecheck (`haxe <hxml>
# --no-output`, the lint oracle) skips every `--cmd`, while it would WRITE the
# output of every block but the last. The line exits with the warm step's
# status, which is always 0 — a failed launcher build or warm leaves a whole
# engine that runs without a cache.
--cmd haxe bin/apq-launch-common.hxml -js bin/apq-launch.js; HXQ_BIN=bin/apq.js sh bin/hxq --warm-code-cache
